@startuml Maintenance-SD-CompleteRecord
autonumber
title US119 — Complete a record stored in another replica (command executed by the owner)
actor "Maintenance\nTechnician" as User
participant "maintenance-1\n: MaintenanceRecordController" as Ctrl
participant "maintenance-1\n: CompleteMaintenanceRecordService" as S1
participant ": PeerClient" as Peers
participant "maintenance-2 (owner)\n: CompleteMaintenanceRecordService" as S2
participant "record : MaintenanceRecord\n(H2 #2)" as Rec <<Entity>>
participant "maintenance-1\n: AircraftAvailabilityService" as Avail
participant "maintenance-2 / -3" as Others
participant "Aircraft Management" as AM

activate User
User -> Ctrl : PATCH /api/maintenance-records/{id}/complete\n(notes, cost, actualDurationMinutes, aircraftFlightHours?)
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> S1 : complete(id, dto)
activate S1
S1 -> S1 : recordRepo.findById(id) → empty
S1 -> Peers : forwardToOwner(PATCH, "/api/maintenance-records/{id}/complete", dto)
activate Peers
Peers -> S2 : PATCH (X-Peer-Hops: 1, X-Service-Key, JWT)
activate S2
S2 -> Rec : complete(CompletionDetails)
activate Rec
note right of Rec
  IN_PROGRESS → COMPLETED (else 409)
  completionDate (default today) >= startDate,
  not in the future; cost >= 0; duration > 0 (else 400)
end note
Rec --> S2
deactivate Rec
S2 -> S2 : saveAndFlush(record)\n(@Version → 409 on a concurrent update)
note right of S2 : peer request: the owner only completes the record\n(it cannot query the other replicas)
S2 --> Peers : 200 MaintenanceRecordDTO (COMPLETED)
deactivate S2
note right of Peers : 404 from a peer = "not mine" → next peer;\n4xx from the owner → same status to the client
Peers --> S1 : MaintenanceRecordDTO
deactivate Peers

S1 -> Avail : releaseIfNoOtherOngoing(reg, id)
activate Avail
Avail -> Avail : local IN_PROGRESS records of reg
Avail -> Others : GET /api/maintenance-records/search?aircraft=reg&status=IN_PROGRESS\n(X-Peer-Hops: 1)
Others --> Avail : []
alt no other ongoing record and every replica answered
    Avail -> AM : PATCH /api/aircrafts/{reg}/status {AVAILABLE} (B3b)
    AM --> Avail : 200
    Avail --> S1 : released = true
else another record ongoing, a replica did not answer, or Aircraft Management failed
    Avail -> Avail : keep UNDER_MAINTENANCE (safe side), log warning
    Avail --> S1 : released = false
end
deactivate Avail
S1 --> Ctrl : Result(record, released)
deactivate S1
Ctrl --> User : 200 OK (MaintenanceRecordDTO)\nX-Aircraft-Released: true | false
deactivate Ctrl
deactivate User

note over User, AM
  A record is only written by its owner replica, so there is a single version of each record.
  The same forwarding is used by US217 (PATCH /component). No owner found → 404.
end note
@enduml
